{"id":"vpoetry","level":6,"levelName":"Reading literature","n":8,"of":11,"title":"The vocabulary of verse","titleHe":"לְשׁוֹן הַשִּׁיר","goal":"The words poems reach for, and their plainer twins.","sections":[{"type":"text","body":"Hebrew poetry has a parallel vocabulary: for almost every ordinary word there is a higher one, and verse alternates between them. Knowing the pairs is half of reading a poem."}],"vocab":[{"he":"לֵבָב","en":"heart (poetic)","translit":"levav"},{"he":"נֶפֶשׁ","en":"soul, self, person","translit":"nefesh"},{"he":"אוֹר","en":"light","translit":"or"},{"he":"חֹשֶׁךְ","en":"darkness","translit":"choshech"},{"he":"שַׁחַר","en":"dawn","translit":"shachar"},{"he":"דִּמְעָה","en":"tear","translit":"dim'a"},{"he":"שִׁיר","en":"song, poem","translit":"shir"},{"he":"קוֹל","en":"voice, sound","translit":"kol"},{"he":"דְּמָמָה","en":"silence, stillness","translit":"dmama"},{"he":"עָפָר","en":"dust","translit":"afar"},{"he":"סֶלַע","en":"rock","translit":"sela"},{"he":"גַּל","en":"wave","translit":"gal"},{"he":"כּוֹכָבִים","en":"stars","translit":"kochavim"},{"he":"רָקִיעַ","en":"firmament, sky","translit":"raki'a"},{"he":"תְּהוֹם","en":"abyss, deep","translit":"tehom"},{"he":"צֵל","en":"shadow","translit":"tsel"},{"he":"לַהַב","en":"flame, blade","translit":"lahav"},{"he":"כְּנַף","en":"wing (construct)","translit":"knaf"},{"he":"מַעֲשֶׂה","en":"deed, work","translit":"ma'ase"},{"he":"פְּרִי","en":"fruit","translit":"pri"},{"he":"שֹׁרֶשׁ","en":"root","translit":"shoresh"},{"he":"נִצָּן","en":"bud","translit":"nitsan"},{"he":"אֵבֶל","en":"mourning","translit":"evel"},{"he":"גִּיל","en":"rejoicing","translit":"gil"},{"he":"כְּאֵב","en":"pain","translit":"ke'ev"},{"he":"עֹז","en":"might","translit":"oz"}],"exercises":[{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["soul","a comma","people, nation","heart (poetic)"],"correct":3,"prompt":"לֵבָב","translit":"levav"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["soul, self, person","life","eng